From 892744348b1334040b84fa22f08e20b218bb0ff5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:00:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] lakeside day clear fix: in dir mode the day pack's
 clearColor is the board init clear (linearToSrgb8(clearColorLinear) =
 #1c8fb8, 28/143/184), not the old hemi-mode LAKESIDE_CLEAR_COLOR #f2b98a

One helper lakesideDayClearColor() (sRGB bytes, never light-encoded; points mode keeps LAKESIDE_CLEAR_COLOR) now feeds the board init clear
(LakesideBoardBackground camera setup), the day pack (board day toggle) and the journey's day end target, so switching to day and the
journey end no longer jump to orange. Light/ambient/water colour conversion and night values untouched. Tests: lakeside-daynight asserts
day clear = board init byte for byte and journey day end (target + w=1) = board init; journey-atmosphere and dirlight follow.
---
